---
import BlogLayout from "../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";

const title = "Indonesia Corporate Income Tax Guide 2026: 22% Rate & SME Discounts";
const description = "Complete guide to Indonesia corporate income tax (PPh Badan). Learn the 22% corporate tax rate, Article 31E 50% SME tax discount, 0.5% turnover tax, and annual corporate SPT 1771 filing.";
const image = "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1486406146926-c627a92ad1ab?w=1200&q=80";
const author = "Bambang Santoso, Certified Indonesian Tax Consultant";
const authorBio = "Certified Indonesian Tax Consultant specializing in corporate tax compliance, PT PMA entity structuring, Article 31E SME tax reductions, and DJP audit defense.";
const canonical = "https://finsiva.com/blogs/indonesia-corporate-tax-guide-2026";

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What is the corporate income tax rate in Indonesia?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "The headline corporate income tax rate in Indonesia is 22% on net taxable profit."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "How does the Article 31E SME corporate tax discount work?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Domestic companies with annual turnover up to IDR 50 billion receive a 50% reduction in the corporate tax rate (effective 11% rate) on taxable income derived from turnover up to IDR 4.8 billion."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What is the 0.5% final turnover tax for small businesses?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Under Government Regulation PP 55/2022, small businesses with annual gross turnover under IDR 4.8 billion can elect to pay a 0.5% final tax on gross monthly turnover instead of standard 22% corporate tax."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What is the annual corporate tax filing deadline in Indonesia?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Corporate taxpayers must submit their annual tax return (SPT Tahunan 1771) online via DJP Online by April 30."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BlogLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  image={image}
  author={author}
  authorBio={authorBio}
  lastUpdated="August 2026"
  readTime="18 min read"
  canonical={canonical}
>
  <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-body dark:text-muted">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
      Operating a domestic company (PT) or foreign direct investment company (PT PMA) in Indonesia requires a thorough understanding of <strong>Indonesian corporate income tax (PPh Badan) rates, small business tax incentives, withholding obligations, and DJP reporting rules</strong>.
    </p>

    <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6 dark:border-overlay-light dark:bg-surface">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3 dark:text-on-primary">Table of Contents</h2>
      <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <li><a href="#headline-rate" class="text-link hover:underline">1. Headline 22% Corporate Tax Rate</a></li>
        <li><a href="#article-31e" class="text-link hover:underline">2. Article 31E 50% Tax Reduction for SMEs</a></li>
        <li><a href="#final-turnover-tax" class="text-link hover:underline">3. 0.5% Final Micro-Business Turnover Tax (PP 55/2022)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#corporate-withholding" class="text-link hover:underline">4. Corporate Withholding Taxes (PPh 23, PPh 4(2))</a></li>
        <li><a href="#spt-1771-deadlines" class="text-link hover:underline">5. Corporate SPT 1771 e-Filing & Deadlines</a></li>
        <li><a href="#faqs" class="text-link hover:underline">6. Frequently Asked Questions</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2 id="headline-rate" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">1. Headline 22% Corporate Tax Rate</h2>
    <p>Administered by the <a href="https://www.pajak.go.id" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline">Direktorat Jenderal Pajak (DJP)</a>, domestic corporations and Permanent Establishments (BUT) are subject to a flat <strong>22% headline corporate income tax rate</strong> on net taxable income.</p>

    <h2 id="article-31e" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">2. Article 31E 50% Tax Reduction for SMEs</h2>
    <p>Under Article 31E of the Income Tax Law, domestic corporations with annual gross turnover up to IDR 50 billion enjoy a <strong>50% tax rate reduction</strong> (resulting in an effective <strong>11% corporate tax rate</strong>) on taxable income derived from turnover up to IDR 4.8 billion.</p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
      <table class="min-w-full border border-hairline text-left text-sm dark:border-overlay-lighter">
        <thead class="bg-canvas-soft font-semibold text-ink dark:bg-surface dark:text-on-primary">
          <tr>
            <th class="border p-3">Annual Corporate Gross Revenue</th>
            <th class="border p-3">Applicable Tax Incentive</th>
            <th class="border p-3">Effective Corporate Tax Rate</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline dark:divide-overlay-lighter">
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 font-medium">Up to IDR 4.8 Billion</td>
            <td class="p-3">Full Article 31E 50% Discount (or 0.5% PP 55)</td>
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-emerald-600">11% (or 0.5% of Gross Turnover)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 font-medium">IDR 4.8 Billion – IDR 50 Billion</td>
            <td class="p-3">Proportional Article 31E 50% Discount</td>
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-emerald-600">Proportional between 11% and 22%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3 font-medium">Exceeding IDR 50 Billion</td>
            <td class="p-3">Standard Headline Corporate Rate</td>
            <td class="p-3 font-semibold">22% Flat Rate</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 id="final-turnover-tax" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">3. 0.5% Final Micro-Business Turnover Tax (PP 55/2022)</h2>
    <p>Small businesses with annual turnover under IDR 4.8 billion can elect to pay a flat <strong>0.5% final tax on gross monthly turnover</strong> for up to 3 years (for PT companies) or 4 years (for CV partnerships) to simplify early tax compliance.</p>

    <h2 id="corporate-withholding" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">4. Corporate Withholding Taxes</h2>
    <p>Indonesian companies act as withholding agents for DJP:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>PPh 23:</strong> 2% withholding tax on domestic services and rental of assets (other than land/buildings), and 15% on dividends/interest paid to resident entities without NPWP penalty.</li>
      <li><strong>PPh 4(2) Final Tax:</strong> 10% final withholding on land/building rental and 2.5% on construction services.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="spt-1771-deadlines" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">5. Corporate SPT 1771 e-Filing & Deadlines</h2>
    <p>Corporate taxpayers must submit their annual tax return (SPT Tahunan 1771) online via DJP Online by <strong>April 30</strong>. Failure to file on time triggers a statutory penalty of IDR 1,000,000.</p>

    <h2 id="faqs" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">6. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What is the corporate tax rate in Indonesia?</h3>
        <p>The headline rate is 22%. SMEs get 50% rate discounts under Article 31E or 0.5% final turnover tax options.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">When is corporate SPT 1771 due?</h3>
        <p>Annual corporate tax returns must be filed electronically by April 30.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6 dark:border-overlay-light dark:bg-surface">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3 dark:text-on-primary">Related Indonesia Corporate & Tax Links</h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
        <a href="/knowledge/indonesia-income-tax/" class="text-link hover:underline font-medium">Indonesia Tax Knowledge Hub</a>
        <a href="/blogs/indonesia-income-tax-rates-brackets-2026/" class="text-link hover:underline font-medium">Personal Tax Rates 2026</a>
        <a href="/blogs/indonesia-capital-gains-dividends-inheritance-tax-guide/" class="text-link hover:underline font-medium">Capital Gains & Dividends Guide</a>
        <a href="/countries/indonesia/income-tax/income-tax-calculator/" class="text-link hover:underline font-medium">Indonesia Tax Calculator</a>
        <a href="/blogs/indonesia-tax-for-expats-foreigners-bali-guide/" class="text-link hover:underline font-medium">Expat & Bali Tax Guide</a>
        <a href="/countries/indonesia/" class="text-link hover:underline font-medium">Finsiva Indonesia Portal</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

          
<div class="mt-12 space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">The Psychology Behind Navigating Indonesia Corporate Income Tax  : 22% Rate & SME Discounts</h2>
  <p>
    Let's be incredibly honest for a moment. When you're trying to understand <strong>Indonesia Corporate Income Tax  : 22% Rate & SME Discounts</strong>, the sheer volume of bureaucratic jargon can feel entirely overwhelming. It’s not just about the numbers or the compliance—it's about the psychological weight of getting it right. Fear of penalties, the stress of audits, and the anxiety of misinterpreting complex regulations are universal pain points.
  </p>
  <p>
    Many taxpayers and business owners experience what financial psychologists call "compliance fatigue." You are expected to be an expert in everything from withholding rules to obscure deduction clauses. The truth is, mastering Indonesia Corporate Income Tax  : 22% Rate & SME Discounts requires a shift in mindset: from reactive compliance to proactive wealth preservation.
  </p>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-6">Advanced Strategies for Minimizing Risk</h3>
  <p>
    Beyond the basic rules, the most successful individuals and corporations employ advanced, legally sound strategies. Here is how you can move from surviving to thriving:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
    <li><strong>Documentation is Your Shield:</strong> Never rely on memory. Maintain granular, digitized records of all expenses, receipts, and correspondence. A well-organized ledger is your best defense against arbitrary assessments.</li>
    <li><strong>Strategic Timing:</strong> The timing of income recognition and expense realization can drastically alter your tax footprint. Accelerating deductions or deferring income into the next fiscal period is a cornerstone of intelligent planning.</li>
    <li><strong>Professional Consultation over DIY:</strong> The cost of an expert is almost always lower than the cost of a compliance error. Navigating Indonesia Corporate Income Tax  : 22% Rate & SME Discounts without professional counsel is an unnecessary risk.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-6">Troubleshooting Common Edge-Case Scenarios</h3>
  <p>
    What happens when things don't go according to plan? Let's address some edge cases that frequently trip up even seasoned professionals when dealing with Indonesia Corporate Income Tax  : 22% Rate & SME Discounts:
  </p>
  <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
    <li><strong>Discrepancies in Source Documents:</strong> If a withholding certificate or an income statement contains errors, do not adjust your return to match the error. Request a formal correction from the issuer immediately.</li>
    <li><strong>Multi-Jurisdictional Conflicts:</strong> If your income crosses borders, you may face double taxation. Always invoke the relevant Double Taxation Avoidance Agreements (DTAA) and ensure you have the necessary tax residency certificates on hand.</li>
    <li><strong>Late Filing Repercussions:</strong> If you miss a deadline, the worst action is inaction. File as soon as possible and proactively request a waiver of penalties citing reasonable cause, if applicable.</li>
  </ol>

  <p class="mt-6 font-medium">
    Ultimately, navigating these regulations is a marathon, not a sprint. By prioritizing structured planning and mental clarity, you can turn a compliance burden into a strategic advantage.
  </p>
</div>

